A||||4||86_Fastback||Cruise Contol
Z||000000||86_Fastback||06-21-99||01:46 PM||||My cruise control hasn't worked since I bought my Fiero last January.  I would appreciate all the information I can get about it.  The Haynes manual doesn't cover it at all.
Z||000001||Cooter||06-21-99||05:48 PM||||Check all the vac. lines going to the Cruise Master, and the electric vac. release valve. Make sure that the release valve is not bleeding off vac. Other than that, all I know to do is to try another unit in its place to see if it works.
Z||000002||SCCA FIERO||06-21-99||05:50 PM||||Mine worked fine until i parked it for 5 years in 93. I got it back on the road and now it doesn't work. The A/C is the same. Why are the convenience things such an inconvenience?
Z||000003||batboy||06-22-99||07:16 PM||||From my experience, a fairly common problem with cruise control is that the rubber part inside the servo unit goes bad.
Z||000004||Lynx||06-23-99||01:17 AM||||To SCCA FIERO, I know this sounds dumb but did you check fuses. Also when a car sits and the Freon in the A/C dosent mix often it always seems to die out, and you need to recharge.
